# Betchen 2006 PLUG high-Re variant, Da=1e-2, Re_H=1000
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Channel y in [0,H] (H=0.01 m); x = 5H fluid | 5H porous | 50H fluid.
# Re_H = rho*U0*H/mu = 1000  =>  U0 = 1000*mu/(rho*H) = 1.5684 m/s
# Dynamic pressure (1/2)rho U0^2 ~ 1.45 Pa (paper quotes 500 for its scale;
# here H=0.01m sets the length).  Da = K/H^2 = 1e-2 => K=1e-6.
# Forchheimer coefficient for eps=0.7:
#   cE = 1.75*eps/(150*eps^5)^0.5 = 0.2440
#   inertial (our convention, rho*inertial*|u|u) = cE/sqrt(K) = 244
# Inlet: paper's fully-developed parabolic profile u(y)=6*U0*(y/H)*(1-y/H)
# (peak 1.5*U0, mean U0) via 'velocity-inlet-parabolic Umean H axis y0 [T]'.
# NB: at Re_H=1000 the developing length is ~50-60H, so the 5H upstream
# segment cannot establish a fully-developed profile before the bed (and the
# zero-gradient outlet sits only 50H downstream): Fig.8 is qualitative only.
# Pore Re_R(=Re_K) ~ U0*sqrt(K)*rho/mu
#   = 1.5684*1e-3*1.177/1.846e-5 = 100  -> Forchheimer now relevant.
mesh_scale = 1.0
rho = 1.177
mu  = 1.846e-5
alpha_u = 0.7
alpha_p = 0.3
outer_max = 4000
outer_tol = 1.0e-8
lin_tol   = 1.0e-8
lin_max   = 200
conv_blend   = 0.0
nonorth_corr = 1.0
ppe_precond  = ic0
inlet_ramp = 1
init_t = 300.0

cell_zone = 3 perm=1.0e-6 inertial=244.0 porosity=0.7

bc = 6 symmetry
bc = 7 wall
bc = 8 wall
bc = 9 velocity-inlet-parabolic 1.5684 0.01 2 0.0 300.0
bc = 10 pressure-outlet 0.0